You are building Feather, a premium Mac stock research app.

ALWAYS:
- Use TypeScript strictly — no 'any' types ever
- Use Tailwind utility classes only — no inline styles, no CSS files
- Use Framer Motion for all animations
- Use components from /src/design-system/ before creating new ones
- Handle loading, error, and empty states on every data-fetching component
- Use Zustand stores for all shared state
- Use custom hooks in /src/hooks/ for all API calls
- Format prices with formatters from /src/lib/formatters.ts
- Use mock data from /src/mocks/ when APIs aren't wired yet

NEVER:
- Use localStorage or sessionStorage
- Hardcode colors — use design tokens from tailwind.config.js
- Call Polygon.io or Claude API directly from components
- Use class components
- Use 'any' TypeScript type
- Create new CSS files
- Use inline styles except for truly dynamic values

DESIGN:
- Background is always #0B0B0F
- Cards use bg-bg-elevated-4, border-border tokens
- Positive numbers: text-status-positive (#4EBE96)
- Negative numbers: text-status-negative (#D84F68)
- Loading states: always use <Skeleton /> component, never spinners
- Animations: subtle, 200-300ms, ease-out. Never flashy.
- Font: Calibre via design tokens
